<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* PulsarComponents' components rely on box-sizing:border-box for their pixel-math layouts
       (PulsarCalendar's time-grid especially) — this reset ships as a plain static asset, not
       something Blazor's per-project scoped-CSS @import chain pulls in automatically, so every
       consuming app must link it explicitly. Missing this produced a genuinely broken calendar
       (oversized rows/misaligned gridlines) before it was traced to this. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/PulsarComponents/pulsar-components.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["PulsarComponents.Sample.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
